1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:11,350
Emily Sanders, a 25-year-old from Detroit, Michigan, set out on December 23rd with high hopes of reaching Toronto to meet her boyfriend for Christmas.

2
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:16,870
Although she had heard warnings about an approaching snowstorm, she didn’t give it much thought.

3
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:24,030
She assumed that much like in Michigan, police would simply detour traffic around any closed sections of the highway.

4
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,060
But that didn’t happen.

5
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:31,140
As the snow came down more and more heavily, Emily was directed off the highway.

6
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:37,210
She drove on for a while and found herself on an unfamiliar road toward a Canadian town.

7
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:40,890
The blinding whiteout made driving nearly impossible.

8
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:44,290
At one point, Emily’s car got stuck.

9
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:50,940
After a struggle, she managed to free the vehicle and continued inching along the snow-covered road.

10
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:53,880
As night fell, panic set in.

11
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:59,150
While Emily was driving on a narrow stretch of road, her car slid into a ditch.

12
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:03,080
She tried to call for help but found no signal on her phone.

13
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:08,310
Seeing no hope of immediate rescue, Emily decided to spend the night in her car.

14
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:12,120
She wrapped herself in a blanket, waiting for morning.

15
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:16,840
To stay warm, she ran her engine for a few minutes every now and then.

16
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,240
Eventually, she fell asleep.

17
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,820
Emily awoke to a gentle knock on her car window.

18
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:30,780
Standing outside were Daniel and his wife Rachel, who noticed the stranded vehicle on their way home and stopped to see if they could help.

19
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:38,740
When Emily rolled down the window, Rachel asked if she was okay and told her it was not safe to stay overnight in the car.

20
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:44,790
With genuine warmth in her voice, Rachel said they could take Emily to a nearby cafe they knew.

21
00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:48,600
Grateful and relieved, Emily accepted the offer.

22
00:01:49,400 --> 00:02:04,000
In the cafe, the couple bought Emily a hot chocolate and listened patiently as she explained her desperate situation: she was about a hundred miles from her destination, her car was completely stuck, and her entire holiday plan could be ruined.

23
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:09,020
Daniel and Rachel suggested that Emily continue her journey by train.

24
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:12,780
Three days later, Emily returned to get her car.
